# How Git should handle line endings.
#
# Without this file Git guesses, and on Windows it kept rewriting files
# on the way in and out. That produced a "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# warning on every commit, and can make Git report that a whole file
# changed when nothing in it actually did.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: store everything with LF line endings, and
# check it out with LF too. Every editor in use here handles LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images are not text. Saying so stops Git ever trying to "fix" them,
# which would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
